							<source><pc id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">To find <ph id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> we look at the sum of the forces in the horizontal direction. In this case <ph id="c3" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> and <ph id="c4" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> have no effect. This gives us the equilibrium equation<ph id="c5" type="ui" subType="swi18n:block-math"/>By decomposing forces we can find that<ph id="c6" type="ui" subType="swi18n:block-math"/>Solving the equilibrium equation for <ph id="c7" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> then gives<ph id="c8" type="ui" subType="swi18n:block-math"/>And with this all support reactions have been determined.</pc></source>
